# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/crossbow.clip: the crossbow (a bow form: `when bow,bow-crossbow`; bow.clip's lines say
# !bow-crossbow) on both bodies (P2c wave 2, ACTIONS-2H; STYLE_P2 25.8 item 6): the drawn idle low across the hips,
# the draw = crank (the follow of the last shot: the nose down, the right hand winding), raise, aim (the stock at the
# shoulder, held as the loaded pose), the release = shoot (the prod snaps, the body kicks back a pixel), the drawn walk
# and run. The bow hand (left) holds the fore-stock: held bow.crossbow at gripL with the keys xlow xaim xshot xcrank
# (WEAPONS draws them). Written by ACTIONS-2H's tools/fams.py.

body man
clip idle D part drawn family bow variant 1 when bow,bow-crossbow
f armL=bw_xlow armR=bw_xlow held=xlow legs=drawn neck=rest sheath=drawn torso=rest bob=1
